---
title: MDX
summary: Markdown with JSX
---

import {Chart} from './snowfall.js'
export const year = 2023

# Last year's snowfall

In {year}, the snowfall was above average. It was followed by a warm spring which caused flood conditions in many of the nearby rivers.

<Chart color="#fcb32c" year={year} />

<Note title="Snowfall">
  This is **markdown** inside {year}.

  - item {year}
  - item <Chart year={year} />
</Note>

{/* An MDX comment */}

An inline expression {items.map((item) => <Chart year={item.year} />)} and object {{year, title: "Snow"}}. A tricky expression {JSON.stringify({ value: "}" })} works.

<Chart
  color="#fcb32c"
  year={year}
/>

`{not an expression} <NotATag>`

```jsx
import {Chart} from './snowfall.js'

<Chart color="#fcb32c" year={2023} />
```

export const meta = {
  title: 'Snowfall',
  year: 2023,
}

